Article 3 (Composition and Functions of the Clinical Research Deliberation Committee)
(1) The National Police Hospital shall establish the National Police Hospital Clinical Research Deliberation Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") to deliberate on major matters concerning clinical research.
(2) The Committee shall consist of not more than five members, including the chairperson, and a secretary, and at least one third of the members shall be external members.
(3) The Director of the National Police Hospital shall appoint the chairperson from among the heads of Clinical Departments I, II, and III of the Hospital, appoint internal members from among public officials at the level of department head or higher in the Hospital, and commission external members from among clinical experts with extensive knowledge and experience. The secretary shall be designated by the chairperson.
(4) The Committee shall deliberate on and coordinate the following matters:
1. Selection of clinical research projects and review of research plans;
2. Evaluation of interim and final reports on clinical research;
3. Payment and recovery of clinical research expenses;
4. Support for clinical research;
5. Other matters concerning clinical research reports.
(5) External members may be paid travel expenses and allowances within the budget: Provided, That no such payment shall be made where an external member who is a public official attends a meeting of the Committee in direct connection with duties under that member's jurisdiction.
